-- title:
--   ℤ_ℓotimesEnd(X)≅ M₂(ℤ_ℓ) for supersingular X
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field, let $p$ be a prime, and assume $k$ has characteristic $p$, is an algebra over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ and is algebraic over it. Let $X$ be a Weierstrass curve over $k$ which is elliptic, and assume the supersingularity hypothesis `hss`: every point $P$ of the associated affine curve with $p \cdot P = 0$ is already $0$, i.e. the $p$-torsion of $X(k)$ is trivial. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \neq p$. Write $R =$ [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalEndSubring k X`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L32) for the subring of the additive endomorphism monoid ring of the points of the base change of $X$ to $k$ generated by those additive endomorphisms that are either zero or rationally represented (the predicate `IsRationallyRepresented`), i.e. the endomorphism ring of $X$ in this formalisation. The assertion is that the type of $\mathbb{Z}_\ell$-algebra isomorphisms $\mathbb{Z}_\ell \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} R \;\cong\; M_2(\mathbb{Z}_\ell)$, the algebra of $2 \times 2$ matrices indexed by `Fin 2` over the $\ell$-adic integers, is nonempty; no particular isomorphism is specified.
--
--   This is the $\ell$-adic half of the determination, due to Deuring and Tate, of the endomorphism ring of a supersingular elliptic curve: away from the characteristic, the endomorphism ring becomes the full matrix algebra $M_2(\mathbb{Z}_\ell)$ after tensoring, which is the local statement saying that $R \otimes \mathbb{Q}$ is a quaternion algebra unramified at every $\ell \neq p$ and that $R$ is locally maximal there. It feeds into the identification of `rationalEndSubring` with a maximal order in a definite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $p$ and $\infty$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_nonempty_padicInt_tensorProduct_rationalEndSubring_algEquiv_matrix.lean

